Newsgroups: alt.comp.acad-freedom.talk
From: U15289@UICVM.UIC.EDU
Subject:  I wec, you wec, we all wec for UWEC :-)
Message-ID: <199305131858.AA10422@eff.org>
Date: Thu, 13 May 1993 18:44:35 GMT

The UWEC AUP reproduced in these pages today says, in pertinent part, that

>   g. Use of computing facilities for personal or business purposes
>      unrelated to the mission of the University.

is actionable.  Prohibiting use of the system for commercial purposes is
one thing; but the "personal purposes" clause, it seems to me, technically
prohibits a wide range of commonplace--and benign--uses.  I refer particularly
to the practice of reading, and posting to, a wide variety of mailing lists
and newsgroups that may not have a provable nexus to the curriculum.  Ironic-
ally, the installation itself makes much of this allegedly illicit activity
possible, by providing the Usenet feed in the first place.  In practice, the
good will and common sense of sysadmins is (usually) likely to minimize
overbreadth in the application of this technicality; but more formal protection
than that, IMHO, would be desirable.

                                                     Mitch Pravatiner
                                                     U15289@uicvm.uic.edu


